WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.738
Lab 2 runs the guide's own commands
in a test tenant, never production.

2
00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.737
The authors haven't run
them, as the page says.

3
00:00:07.737 --> 00:00:13.487
You need Module 1's test tenant, in the
worldwide or G C C cloud; for G C C High or

4
00:00:13.487 --> 00:00:19.425
D O D, create the rule in the portal from
the file instead of steps four and five.

5
00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:24.416
You need an account with Detection
tuning, manage, or Security Administrator,

6
00:00:24.416 --> 00:00:27.769
activated through pim, and
Defender for Identity or

7
00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:30.888
Cloud Apps connected, for
step six to return rows.

8
00:00:30.888 --> 00:00:34.949
Step one connects with the hunting
and custom detection permissions.

9
00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:40.062
Step two writes the guide's example rule
to a file, with its status disabled.

10
00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:45.025
The slide shortens it; the page has the
whole file, exactly as the guide gives it.

11
00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:49.987
Step three reads the file back and runs
its query against the last thirty days,

12
00:00:49.987 --> 00:00:52.700
saving the output as
the rule's test record.

13
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.825
In a quiet test tenant it returns no rows.

14
00:00:55.825 --> 00:00:58.125
That shows the known-good window only.

15
00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:01.970
A rule isn't finished until its
known-bad event is shown to fire.
